  "terms": {
    "version": "2026-09-05",
    "summary": "CHARON is a supplementary instrument and every answer is an evaluative estimate from public on-chain data at the moment of the call - not a guarantee, an audit or a recommendation. Crypto collateral is volatile and an oracle can move between two reads: verify against your lender's own interface before acting, and never rely on this alone.",
    "advisory": "This is a supplementary instrument. Every answer is an evaluative estimate computed from public on-chain data at the moment of the call - not an audit, not a guarantee, and not a recommendation to open, hold or close a position. Read it beside your lender's own interface and your own numbers; do not rely on it alone.",
    "volatility": "Crypto collateral is volatile. A price can move further in one minute than a daily reading assumes over a week, and an oracle can be updated - or deliberately pushed - between two of our reads. A watch is best effort: it goes out when we manage to read the chain and reach you, and it is never a promise that you will be warned in time, or at all. Being liquidated is a normal outcome of borrowing against a volatile asset, and you can lose all of the collateral.",
    "data_limits": "We see what public RPC endpoints will tell us, through adapters for the venues we index. A market we do not index, a chain we do not serve or a protocol that prices collateral differently will read as missing rather than as safe, and a route quote is a quote, not a fill.",
    "not_advice": "Nothing here is investment, financial, tax or legal advice, and no answer is warranted fit for any purpose. The position, the keys and the decision stay yours.",
    "url": "https://charon.independentai.network/#terms"
  },
  "disclaimer": "CHARON is a supplementary instrument and every answer is an evaluative estimate from public on-chain data at the moment of the call - not a guarantee, an audit or a recommendation. Crypto collateral is volatile and an oracle can move between two reads: verify against your lender's own interface before acting, and never rely on this alone.",
  "description": "Liquidation risk read from the liquidator's own machinery, pointed at the borrower. Exact integer kill prices across Aave-family, Compound-family and Morpho Blue; a real route quote for the collateral a liquidator would actually have to sell; and the one nobody else answers - which contracts your collateral price is read out of, and how often anyone writes to them. Answers about a position or market you name; publishes no ranking of who is cheapest to break.",
